{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovLevelR","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovLevelR","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovAssembly","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlMarkovCorner"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markov_wenzlWeight_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markov_wenzlWeight_two","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovLevelR.lean#L67-L93","doc":"**Conservativity: at `r = 2` this *is* the merged convention-D statement.**\n\n`z_2 = (q²)²/(q·[2]_{q²}) = q³/(q²+1) = z_D` and `wenzlWeight 2 (q²) = ocneanuWeight q z_D`, so\n`markov_wenzlWeight` at `r = 2` reproduces `MarkovConventionD.markov_conventionD` on the nose — the\ngeneral-level theorem specialises back to what #5575 proved, rather than merely resembling it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markov_wenzlWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.markov_wenzlWeight","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WenzlMarkovLevelR.lean#L44-L65","doc":"**The Markov condition for `wenzlWeight r (q²)`, at every integer level `r`.**\n\nThe `w`-weighted seminormal trace of `ι y · σ_{m+1}` over the diagrams of size `m + 2` is `z_r` times\nthe `w`-weighted trace of `y` over those of size `m + 1`, with\n\n`z_r = Q^r / (q · [r]_Q)`,  `Q = q²`.\n\n`hgen` — `Q` is not a root of unity — is the single genericity hypothesis the whole level-`r` chain\nruns on; `hq2` is what `seminormalRep` itself needs, and is implied by `hgen` but has to be named\nbecause it appears in the statement. ","signatureChunk":0}]}